{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.TwistSeparationContent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistSeparationContent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.BigOperators","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistContent.twist_dilemma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistContent.twist_dilemma","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistSeparationContent.lean#L138-L150","doc":"The dilemma, as a single statement: for any candidate twist on words,\n*either* it factors through the writhe — and then it is constant on\nwrithe-degenerate pairs, separating nothing — *or* it does not, in which case it\ncarries information the crossing content does not determine, and that\ninformation was supplied by hand rather than derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistContent.factoring_twist_cannot_separate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistContent.factoring_twist_cannot_separate","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistSeparationContent.lean#L124-L136","doc":"**The other horn.**  A twist determined by the crossing content — i.e.\nfactoring through the writhe, as a canonical ribbon twist does — takes equal\nvalues on writhe-degenerate states, so it separates nothing.\n\nThis is `chirality_not_a_function_of_crossing` (V9) applied to the twist: a\ndatum that factors through a coordinate cannot separate states sharing it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistContent.separation_holds_with_one_word","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistContent.separation_holds_with_one_word","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistSeparationContent.lean#L111-L122","doc":"**The claim survives collapsing the braid group to a point.**\n\n`Word := Unit` has one element, so there is a single word and the writhe is\nconstant. Separation still holds. Whatever this establishes, it is not about\nbraids. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistContent.separation_at_fixed_word","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistContent.separation_at_fixed_word","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistSeparationContent.lean#L88-L109","doc":"**The docstring's claim, with the word in the type.**\n\nAt a *fixed* word `β`, two framings of `β` have different total twist — so the\npair is writhe-degenerate by construction (same word, hence same writhe).\n\nNote the binders: `Word` is an arbitrary type and `writhe` an arbitrary\nfunction, both entirely unused in the proof. That is the finding — the sentence\nis provable without knowing what a braid is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistContent.totalTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistContent.totalTwist","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistSeparationContent.lean#L85-L86","doc":"Total twist. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistContent.TwistDatum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistContent.TwistDatum","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistSeparationContent.lean#L81-L83","doc":"Per-strand integer framing datum (the model used by `def:strand-twist-datum`:\nan arbitrary function, unconstrained by any braid). ","signatureChunk":0}]}